    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d626">

                <pb facs="0527" n="515" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg515"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00114A European War 1939/102: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé at Tangier</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Childs</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tangier</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-11-10T22:00:00+01:00">November 10,
                            1942—10 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 10—3:56 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>584. The 19 American aviators and soldiers mentioned in my 582 of November 10
                    landed at the air drome in Tetuán early on November 8 after losing their way and
                    running short of petrol. They were forced off their course by AA fire. Their
                    plane was landed in perfect condition and is now under guard of the Spanish
                    authorities.</p>
                <p>The Lieutenant in command informed me privately that it was his understanding
                    that he was not to destroy his instruments in a neutral country and
                    unfortunately he had not undertaken this. The plane is a troop carrier.</p>
                <p>Please instruct urgently what representations if any I should make concerning the
                    status of this plane.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Childs</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
